      "weather": "overcast",
      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "GOLDEN CLOUD (1) returns for the Jolly & Potter camp. Was well found in his debut prep and while he couldn't get off the mark he was far from disgraced with two encouraging efforts is some strong maidens. Looks to have come on nicely during the break, fitted with two hitouts. Is drawn favourably and keeps gun hoop in Toeroek from his most recent trial. Expecting him to shed the maiden tag. PAY DIRT (2) is the obvious main danger after just missing on debut at Murray Bridge where he was doing his best work late. Is sure to have come on from that. VIA NICCOLINA (9) was good first-up behind Whiskey Tumbler, who has since gone and won again. Raced greenly second-up in the slop on the Parks track and failed to get involved. Willing to give her another look third-up. SETTLE PETAL (6) has hit the line nicely in her last two and should be hitting her straps now fourth-up. Still needs to go up a rung or two though. Debutant TRAPEZE QUEEN (8) can also play a role.",
